<title>SWEDEN: SCA first quarter profit falls 12 pct.</title>
<headline>SCA first quarter profit falls 12 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry group SCA released the following figures for the first quarter of 1997 ended March 31.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		    894 vs  1,014</p>
<p> Net sales				  14,216 vs 14,732</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	    2.62 vs  3.07</p>
<p> Operating costs			  12,142 vs 12,580</p>
<p> Depreciation				  952 vs    896</p>
<p> Associated interest			   7 vs	9</p>
<p> Operating profit			  1,129 vs  1,265</p>
<p> Net financial items	   CHARGE    235 vs    251 CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					     295 vs    334</p>
<p> Minorities				     82 vs     73</p>
<p> Net profit				    517 vs    607</p>
<p>NOTE -- The forecast for SCA's first quarter results was for a profit of 950 million crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
